    "description": "Senior Performance Software Engineer at Hewlett Packard Enterprise with 5+ years of experience improving the performance, scalability, and reliability of large-scale distributed storage systems. I specialize in profiling and optimizing systems across CPU, memory, I/O, and networking, translating deep technical insights into measurable product and business impact.\n\nIn my current role, I lead performance investigations and performance regression testing for production workloads, drive kernel and filesystem performance analysis, and build predictive models for complex distributed I/O patterns. My work has directly enabled multiple multimillion-dollar sales by partnering with sales and product teams to validate performance claims and address customer concerns before purchase.\n\nPreviously as an SDET, I built automated test frameworks and full-stack tools (Python, C++, React, Django, Kafka) to orchestrate large-scale integration and failure-injection testing. I collaborated closely with developers to debug system-level issues across kernel drivers and storage layers, helping improve durability, recovery, and overall system stability.\n\nAcross roles, I’m known for \n- bridging engineering, product, and sales\n- mentoring engineers in performance best practices\n- turning complex performance data into clear, actionable decisions.",
